{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For all the men are dead.</b> We say in tractate ע\"ז: What are these 'men'? Datan and Aviram. And yet they were alive, but they had descended from their wealth, and a poor person is considered as dead. And if you say they were metzoraim or blind — for we say: four are considered as dead: a blind person, a metzora, a poor person, and one who has no children — one can say: certainly they were not metzoraim, for we do not find that they were sent outside the camp. And blind they were not either, as it is said: ״העיני האנשים ההם תנקר״ etc. And they were not without children, as it is written: ״ובניהם ונשיהם וטפם״. And if you ask: still, perhaps there was one of them among these, and these verses were written after the giving of the Torah — ״וכל העם״ etc. — for their blemishes were healed at Sinai. One can say: if it was before the giving of the Torah, even if they were healed they returned to their blemishes through the sin of the calf, and these verses were written after that deed. And if you ask: still, say they had no children, and what is written ״ובניהם״ was born later — one can say: those who are destined to beget children would not be called dead. Furthermore, one can say: it is necessary to say they had descended from their wealth and had no power to harm anyone — for if you say they were rich, and they are called 'dead' on account of other matters, he would still have had to fear lest they give money to kill him. Rather, certainly they had descended from their wealth. And also: מת\"ו in gematria equals ירד\"ו מנכסיה\"ם deficient by one, from the R. Moshe z\"l."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The abbreviation ע\"ז resolved as tractate Avodah Zarah; the gematria observation and its arithmetic (מת\"ו vs ירד\"ו מנכסיה\"ם 'deficient by one') are rendered exactly as written without verification."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:45.665235846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}